%description:

Tests that a socket command which reaches an EthernetLayer without socket
support (hasSocketSupport = false, the default) stops the simulation with an
error. The EthernetSocketIo of an EthernetSinkApp binds its socket at startup.
Without socket support, the layer has no socket command processor, so the BIND
request reaches the MAC header inserter.

Before the inserter rejected socket commands, it passed the request down to
the node's dispatcher, which dispatched it to the ethernetmac service, back up
to the same layer, and the request circled at t = 0 until the CPU time limit
ended the run.

%# expected-result: FAIL

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib
include ../../lib/socket-command.ini

*.host2.numApps = 1
*.host2.app[0].typename = "EthernetSinkApp"
*.host2.app[0].io.interface = "eth0"
*.host2.app[0].io.localAddress = "host2"

%subst: /\x1B\[[0-9;]*m//
%exitcode: 1
%postrun-command: grep "<!>" test.* > test_err.out || true
%contains: test_err.out
Received socket command BIND, but the protocol layer has no socket support (hasSocketSupport = false)
